structor is trivial, use…"]],0,72],[7147124,20434,125,3.338,2.753,[[5,26]],[["2b422ee4_ba6920ee",20,-16,1,"Can we avoid hard coding these values?"],["ae812f72_9fd23151",20,-16,1,"How to support other EPs?"],["8dc77309_0ca6ef87",3,-10,1,"Could you please also explain why this is necessary? For example, share your command line to run fuzz test on ORT?"],["c6ea0228_695f408d",21,-10,1,"Are these two headers inclusions necessary?"],["20f54825_c15ab2b0",20,-8,0,"Are you able to use `GpuHostInterceptorForTesting` found in gpu_host.mojom-test-utils.h instead of making your own."],["4a9ddd32_12c0d0b8",21,-8,1,"```suggestion FakeGpuHostForTesting fake_gpu_host_; ```"],["f13ae845_1cc97421",22,-8,1,"```suggestion scoped_feature_list_.InitFromCommandLine( command_line->GetSwitchValueASCII(switches::kEnableFeatures), command_line->GetSwitchValueASCII(switches::kDisableFeatures)); ```"],["ca38b950_2d18a9b6",20,-2,0,"Why do we need to #include dxgi_info.mojom.h?"]],0,73],[7244911,20434,29,0.518,0.377,[[1,0.907,38,26],[0,0.093,18,3]],[["87a862e9_0f5334c1",3,-2,0,"If this issue only exists in default CPU EP, we may consider limiting it only."],["9b2ff426_73e82476",3,-2,0,"Could we emulate int32 input support if the zero points is not all zero values constant or is an input operand."]],0,74],[7292070,20445,23,0.969,0.781,[[5,27]],[],0,75]]}